{"cuisine/pacific-northwest-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/pacific-northwest-cuisine","n":"Pacific Northwest cuisine","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Western American cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-western-united-states"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in United States of America","intro":[["Pacific Northwest cuisine is a North American cuisine that is found in the Pacific Northwest, i.e. the states of Oregon, Washington, Idaho and Alaska, as well as the province of British Columbia and the southern portion of the territory of Yukon,  reflecting the ethnic makeup of the region, with noticeable influence from Asian and Native American traditions. Influences from Southern cuisine brought by African Americans, as well as Mexican-American cuisine as Latinos migrate north from California, can be seen as well."],["Seattle's Pike Place Market is notable regarding this culinary style, along with Portland and Vancouver. Former food critic of The New York Times Frank Bruni wrote of Seattle in June 2011, \"I'm hard-pressed to think of another corner or patch of the United States where the locavore sensibilities of the moment are on such florid (and often sweetly funny) display, or where they pay richer dividends, at least if you're a lover of fish.\""]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"pacific-northwest-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pacific_Northwest_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Western American cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-western-united-states"]]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":3,"rows":[{"name":"The Northwest Essentials Cookbook","ref":"cookbook/the-northwest-essentials-cookbook","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Greg Atkinson","note":"Cooking with the ingredients that define Pacific Northwest regional cuisine, by a Seattle chef and writer.","url":"","suggested":true},{"name":"Pure Flavor: 125 Fresh All-American Recipes from the Pacific Northwest","ref":"cookbook/pure-flavor-125-fresh-all-american-recipes-from-the-pacific-northwest","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Kurt Beecher Dammeier, 2007","note":"Regional recipes from the founder of Seattle's Beecher's Handmade Cheese.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/9780307346421","suggested":true},{"name":"PNW Veg","ref":"cookbook/pnw-veg","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Kim O'Donnel","note":"Seasonal vegetarian recipes built on Pacific Northwest produce.","url":"https://penguinrandomhouse.com/books/isbn/9781632170538","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Dishes","count":2,"links":[["Paley's Place","dish/paley-s-place"],["Seattle-style hot dog","dish/seattle-style-hot-dog"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Bialy","ingredient/bialy"],["Bialy (bread)","ingredient/bialy-bread"],["Cream cheese","ingredient/cream-cheese"],["Hot dog","ingredient/hot-dog"],["Hot dog bun","ingredient/hot-dog-bun"],["Sautéed onions","ingredient/sauteed-onions"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Western American cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-western-united-states"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/d4/Alaskan_ceviche.jpg/500px-Alaskan_ceviche.jpg","w":500,"h":616,"by":"Beeblebrox","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alaskan_ceviche.jpg"}},"dish/adobo-filipino-dish":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/adobo-filipino-dish","n":"Adobo (Filipino dish)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 3 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Adobo is a popular Filipino dish and cooking process in Philippine cuisine. In its base form, meat, seafood, or vegetables are first browned in oil, and then marinated and simmered in vinegar, salt and/or soy sauce, and garlic. It is often considered the unofficial national dish in the Philippines."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-adobo-filipino-dish"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adobo_(Filipino_dish)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Filipino cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine"],["Mindanao cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-mindanao"],["Visayan cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-visayas"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Bay leaf","ingredient/bay-leaf"],["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Soy sauce","ingredient/soy-sauce"],["Vinegar","ingredient/vinegar"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Panlasang Pinoy","ref":"site/panlasangpinoy-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"panlasangpinoy.com","note":"Vanjo Merano's large library of Filipino recipes and cooking videos.","url":"https://panlasangpinoy.com/filipino-food/","suggested":true},{"name":"Kawaling Pinoy","ref":"site/kawalingpinoy-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"kawalingpinoy.com","note":"Lalaine Manalo's blog of Filipino home cooking.","url":"https://www.kawalingpinoy.com/about/","suggested":true},{"name":"Flavours of Iloilo","ref":"site/flavoursofiloilo-blogspot-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"flavoursofiloilo.blogspot.com","note":"Blog of Ilonggo home dishes from Iloilo in the Western Visayas.","url":"https://flavoursofiloilo.blogspot.com/2013/05/how-about-some-chicken-binakol.html","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Filipino cuisine","links":[["Aparon","dish/aparon"],["Banana ketchup","dish/banana-ketchup"],["Champorado","dish/champorado"],["Classic Savory","dish/classic-savory"],["Filipino barbecue","dish/filipino-barbecue"],["Food for the gods","dish/food-for-the-gods"],["Isaw","dish/isaw"],["Kadyos, baboy, kag langka","dish/kadyos-baboy-kag-langka"],["Kadyos, manok, kag ubad","dish/kadyos-manok-kag-ubad"],["Kumukunsi","dish/kumukunsi"],["Mango float","dish/mango-float"],["Palapa (condiment)","dish/palapa-condiment"],["Pastil","dish/pastil"],["Piaparan","dish/piaparan"],["Pilipit","dish/pilipit"],["Piyanggang manok","dish/piyanggang-manok"],["Sushi bake","dish/sushi-bake"],["Tortang talong","dish/tortang-talong"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/38/Chicken_adobo.jpg/500px-Chicken_adobo.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"dbgg1979 on flickr","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chicken_adobo.jpg"}},"ingredient/red-bell-pepper":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/red-bell-pepper","n":"Red bell pepper","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["The bell pepper (also known as sweet pepper, paprika, pepper, capsicum  or, in some parts of the U.S. Midwest, mango) is the fruit of plants in the Grossum Group of the species Capsicum annuum. Cultivars of the plant produce fruits in different colors, including red, yellow, orange, green, white, and purple. Bell peppers are sometimes grouped with less pungent chili varieties as \"sweet peppers\". While they are botanically fruits—classified as berries—they are commonly used as a vegetable ingredient or side dish. Other varieties of the genus Capsicum are categorized as chili peppers when they are cultivated for their pungency, including some varieties of Capsicum annuum."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-red-bell-pepper"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_bell_pepper"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Portuguese cuisine","cuisine/portuguese-cuisine",[["Bacalhau à Zé do Pipo","dish/bacalhau-a-ze-do-pipo"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Bacalhau","ingredient/bacalhau"],["Bay leaf","ingredient/bay-leaf"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Mashed potato","ingredient/mashed-potato"],["Mashed potatoes","ingredient/mashed-potatoes"],["Mayonnaise","ingredient/mayonnaise"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Olive","ingredient/olive"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Olives","ingredient/olives"],["Onion","ingredie